Kourier patch 0002: TDLib never answers an incoming call.

Applied by `cargo xtask tdlib build` to TDLib commit 0e88653dcbf4e44c73cb655a05b58cd749a91169 before
the build, after 0001 (`git apply --check`, then `git apply`); listed in third_party/tdlib/tdlib.pin
and part of the cache key and the manifest (the patch's sha256 is a key input: a change of these bytes
is another cache entry).

What it disables: td/telegram/CallManager.cpp, `CallManager::update_call`. Unpatched, an
`updatePhoneCall` with `phoneCallRequested` (someone calls the account) makes a `CallActor` for the
call at once, with no request of the app. That actor sends `phone.receivedCall` right away
(CallActor.cpp `send_received_query`), and on an error there, or when its ring or receive timeout
runs out, it ends the call with `phone.discardCall` and the reason Missed (`on_error`,
`try_send_discard_query`, `timeout_expired`). So every account linked to Kourier would tell Telegram
"received" for every incoming 1:1 call and could END the caller's call as "missed" on the account's
other devices. Kourier shows calls and never takes them (its calls rule: never a reply on the wire),
and the helper's forbidden list cannot stop this, because no app request is involved.

With the patch an incoming call gets NO call actor: no `updateCall` reaches the app, no
`phone.receivedCall`, no `phone.discardCall`, no DH config request, no timeout. Later updates of that
call (`phoneCallDiscarded`) find no actor and take TDLib's existing "postpone" branch right below the
hunk, as TDLib already does for a call it never saw ringing. The call rings on the account's other
devices and ends there; Kourier shows it from the chat's `messageCall` service message. Outgoing and
group calls are untouched (Kourier makes none; the helper forbids the call requests).

What it costs: one small `call_info_` entry (with the postponed updates of that call) per incoming
call for the helper's life.

Second hunk, the run-time marker: td/telegram/OptionManager.cpp, `get_synchronous_options` and
`get_option_synchronously`. TDLib answers a SYNCHRONOUS option `kourier_patch_level` (beside `version` and
`commit_hash`; `td_execute` of `getOption` before any client exists, and an `updateOption` in the first
updates like the other two) with the value "0002": the newest Kourier patch in the library. Each later
Kourier patch changes this one value in its own hunk. The helper reads it before the hello and the app's
`check_pin` refuses any other value or none, so a stock, 0001-only or pre-0002 library is refused before
any client exists, wherever it was found. It costs one more entry in the synchronous option table.

The context lines are TDLib's (Boost Software License 1.0, LICENSES/BSL-1.0.txt); so is this file.

--- a/td/telegram/CallManager.cpp
+++ b/td/telegram/CallManager.cpp
